## Title: Under Pressure
## Author: Th3rtythr33
## Version: 0.3.3
## AddOnVersion: 13
## APIVersion: 101049 101050
## SavedVariables: UnderPressureSavedVars
## DependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings
## Description: Quickly see how much danger you are in and how long you have to live if the damage isn't healed through or mitigated. Also provides a counter of how many distinct mobs you are taking damage from.

; AddOnVersion tracks the LAST PUBLISHED build. 0.2.7 = 8, 0.2.8 = 9,
; 0.2.9 = 10, 0.3.0 = 11, 0.3.2 = 12, so 0.3.3 = 13. It must only ever increase -- it
; steps by one per published build regardless of how far the semantic
; ## Version jumps. It was briefly set to 30 while the release was planned as
; 3.0; that build was never published, so stepping back to 9 was safe and
; would NOT have been safe if 30 had shipped.
;
; The Tank Mode sentence was dropped from the Description in 0.2.9 along with
; the feature. The Bethesda.net web listing carries its own copy of this text
; and has to be edited separately, in the uploader -- it is not derived from
; this file.
;
; The settings library changed in 0.3.3: LibAddonMenu-2.0 -> LibHarvensAddonSettings.
; LAM does resolve on console, but its console support is a partial
; auto-conversion INTO LibHarvensAddonSettings and not every control type
; survives it; depending on LHAS directly drops the conversion layer. See
; Docs/UnderPressure.md.
;
; DependsOn (not Optional) is correct: LibHarvensAddonSettings IS listed on the
; Bethesda.net console catalogue under its own name, confirmed by the author
; 2026-08-01, so the dependency resolves and gets auto-installed there. Do not
; "fix" this to OptionalDependsOn -- that was tried in 0.2.8 development (for
; LAM) on the mistaken belief that the library was unavailable on console, and
; it would cost users the auto-install and therefore the settings panel
; entirely.
;
; Ignore the "For Console" note on LibHarvensAddonSettings' ESOUI project page
; telling you to depend on LibVotans instead. That dates from a bogus DMCA
; takedown; the Bethesda.net listing has since been restored under the original
; name, and the manifest name was never the thing that changed anyway.
;
; No version bound on the dependency. Nothing used here is specific to a recent
; LHAS release, and a bound could only produce a false negative against
; whatever AddOnVersion the Bethesda.net copy happens to report.
;
; The Description directive above must stay a SINGLE line (manifest
; directives cannot wrap) and should match the Bethesda.net listing copy.
; Note the two render differently: the Bethesda.net web listing takes a
; markdown-like syntax, while the IN-GAME add-on browser uses ESO's own
; |cRRGGBB|r colour codes. Plain text like this is the safe intersection.

; Load order: bootstrap -> engine -> UI -> settings -> main entry
; Fonts.lua must load before any UI that sets a font.

Engine/FeatureDetect.lua
Engine/AbilityClassifier.lua
Engine/AttackerTracker.lua
Engine/SilenceTracker.lua
Engine/PressureEngine.lua
Engine/EventIngest.lua

UI/Fonts.lua
UI/Indicator.xml
UI/Indicator.lua
UI/SilenceRing.xml
UI/SilenceRing.lua
UI/Debug.xml
UI/Debug.lua

Settings.lua

UnderPressure.lua
